A||||11||overlord||duke making weird noise.||||1||
Z||000000||overlord||03-19-2001||08:00 AM||||in the fall, i noticed my 84 duke was making an odd noise. The car runs great but has this  ticking noise coming somewhere from the engine.  It seems to only do it when i accelerate normally....give it some gas and the ticking goes away.  And when im cruising at highway speeds it doesnt do it either...just when i accelerate normally.<P>Ill stop by the mechanics today and see what they say.......just wanted to see if anyone else might have an idea?<P>||||reg||1
Z||000001||LottaBallsCamaro||03-19-2001||09:16 AM||||It could very well be a rod knocking. When your at highway speeds or under hard acceleration, the engine will drownd out the knock. It could also be a rocker arm out of adjusment. Where is the noise most prevalent. if its in the bottem end, its probably the rod bearings. If its in the vavle cover, you need to have your valvves adjusted. How is your oil pressure?<P>------------------<BR>91'RS 305TBI no mods to date<BR>92' Lumina 275,000 miles and still humping!!!!||||reg||1
Z||000002||overlord||03-19-2001||10:17 AM||||oil presure?  no idea.  I dont have the guaage.  And i cant really tell where its coming from cause you cant hear it when its just idling.  Like i said, under normal acceleration.   It  could very well be a rod or something like that, cause this noise happened after we did the head gasket ourselves.<P>Ill find out for sure after lunch.||||reg||1
Z||000003||862M4inCA||03-19-2001||01:36 PM||||In my experience if a rod is going then you will usually hear the noise even at idle. I'd be willing to bet the noise is most likely coming from somewhere inside the valve train. If the sound was also occuring at idle I'd suggest pulling plug wires (and grounding them somewhere of course) and see if the noise stopped....would be an easy way to help determine if a rod was the case since a rod can't knock as loud if it's not being forced down if it's not firing.||||reg||1
Z||000004||KRMFiero||03-19-2001||02:48 PM||||I know what sound your talking about, it is not a rod knock, a rod will shake your car and stuff and is alot louder - you would be afraid to drive it.<P>My 85 is making the same tick, i'm not sure what it is but i think it is eather a valve or something, it could also be somthing with the Tranny or clutch (Something broke in mine the other day) so umm you might want to get it looked at, i dont know exactly what it is though<P>Kyle||||reg||1
Z||000005||StuGood||03-19-2001||02:52 PM||||Take off the oil filler cap while it's idling (briefly - and don't let too much oil splatter out) - if the ticking gets louder and seems to come from the oil-fill hole in the valve cover - it's probably a valvetrain (lifter/rocker adjustment) problem. ||||reg||3
Z||000006||862M4inCA||03-19-2001||03:42 PM||||Something just dawned on me. I had an annoying tick from my engine recently that lead me to believe I might have a flat spot in the cam. The noise started out as a slight tick, maybe like a valve needed adjusting. Well over the course of a couple weeks it started getting worse. Decided to check things out and low and behold the bolt holding on the harmonic balancer loosened up. I guess the sound I was hearing was the timing gear. After giving the bolt a few quick turns and a good snug down in the parking lot at work (was having a quick smoke break when I checked it out) the noise stopped and hasn't been back. Might just be something to look at.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Fierowrecker||03-19-2001||06:27 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by overlord:<BR><B>in the fall, i noticed my 84 duke was making an odd noise. The car runs great but has this  ticking noise coming somewhere from the engine.  It seems to only do it when i accelerate normally....give it some gas and the ticking goes away.  And when im cruising at highway speeds it doesnt do it either...just when i accelerate normally.<P>Ill stop by the mechanics today and see what they say.......just wanted to see if anyone else might have an idea?<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I had the same type of noise, it turned out to be a piston skirt had cracked...<BR>When it let loose, it cracked the cylinder wall...<BR>Lots of smoke!!!<BR>crash...||||reg||1
Z||000008||LottaBallsCamaro||03-19-2001||11:01 PM||||Its probably valvetrain noise. If its the rocker arms, they are fairly easy to adjust yourself. 2.8's are notorious for wiping cam lobes but I dont know how it wold make a tick. A rod knock doesnt have to be loud in the early stages. If it is a knock, it will gradualy get worse until it does feel unsafe to drive.||||reg||1
Z||000009||LuckyTheyWereEverMade||03-20-2001||12:46 AM||||Are you sure it isn't an exhaust leak:<P>cracked manifold<BR>leaking EGR valve gasket<BR>exhaust maniflod gasket<BR>rusty/damaged exhaust pipe, cat converter, or muffler<BR>Bad "donut" gasket between header and tailpipe.<P>Leaks at any of these places can sound like a metallic tapping sound.  They can go from pretty quiet to really loud with the throttle opened up (under acceleration).<P>If you're lucky, it's just a gasket . . .<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000010||862M4inCA||03-20-2001||01:04 AM||||I would have suggested an exhaust leak, but when I read the post it sounded to ME like if he was just accelerating (under normal conditions) it was present, but under harder acceleration it wasn't there. In my experience a hard acceleration makes the noise more prominant which leads me to believe it's mechanical. ||||reg||1
Z||000011||Kelvin Vivian||03-20-2001||01:55 PM||||make sure you are not missing any waterpump bracket bolts... An 85 Fiero 4-cyl that I used to have ticked in rear due to these missing bolts..<P>Kelvin Vivian<BR>87 Fiero SE, med red/grey, 5-spd<BR>88 Fiero GT, red/tan, 5-spd||||reg||1
